.TH "MINIOS\-LIVE" "1" "September 2026" "MiniOS Live System Builder" ""
.SH NAME
minios\-live \- build MiniOS ISO images in ordered stages
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]minios\-live\f[R] [\f[B]\-h\f[R] | \f[B]\-\-help\f[R]]
[\f[I]start\-command\f[R]] [\f[B]\-\f[R]] [\f[I]end\-command\f[R]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\f[B]minios\-live\f[R] builds a MiniOS live system as an ordered
sequence of stages.
It creates a base system, layered SquashFS modules, boot files,
configuration data, and the final ISO.
.PP
The default \f[B]build.conf\f[R] currently lists Debian
\f[B]buster\f[R], \f[B]bullseye\f[R], \f[B]bookworm\f[R], and
\f[B]trixie\f[R]; Ubuntu \f[B]bionic\f[R], \f[B]focal\f[R],
\f[B]jammy\f[R], \f[B]noble\f[R], and \f[B]resolute\f[R]; and Devuan
\f[B]beowulf\f[R], \f[B]chimaera\f[R], \f[B]daedalus\f[R], and
\f[B]excalibur\f[R].
It lists \f[B]amd64\f[R], \f[B]i386\f[R], and \f[B]i386\-pae\f[R]
architectures; \f[B]core\f[R], \f[B]flux\f[R], \f[B]xfce\f[R], and
\f[B]lxqt\f[R] environments; \f[B]minimum\f[R], \f[B]standard\f[R],
\f[B]toolbox\f[R], and \f[B]ultra\f[R] variants; and \f[B]xz\f[R],
\f[B]lzo\f[R], \f[B]gz\f[R], \f[B]lz4\f[R], and \f[B]zstd\f[R]
compression.
.PP
Not every combination is necessarily available.
The installed configuration, selected environment, and configured
repositories determine what can be built.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
Build stages require root.
Help does not.
.PP
A source\-tree build requires a Debian or Ubuntu host and the packages
listed in \f[B]linux\-live/prerequisites.list\f[R].
Repository access must be available directly or through the configured
cache.
The default configuration enables apt\-cacher\-ng at
\f[B]127.0.0.1:3142\f[R]; run that service or set
\f[B]USE_APT_CACHER=false\f[R].
.PP
Do not run internal scripts from the \f[B]linux\-live\f[R] directory
directly.
.PP
The current bootstrap uses \f[B]debootstrap \[en]no\-check\-gpg\f[R] and
retrieves some repository keys over unauthenticated HTTP.
Independently verify build inputs before treating a locally built image
as a trusted release artifact.
.SH COMMANDS
Commands run in the following order.
Hyphens and underscores are interchangeable in command names.
.TP
\f[B]build\-bootstrap\f[R]
Recreate the selected target\[cq]s \f[B]core\f[R] and \f[B]image\f[R]
trees, then create or restore the minimal root filesystem.
.TP
\f[B]build\-chroot\f[R]
Install and configure core system components in the chroot.
.TP
\f[B]build\-live\f[R]
Create the core SquashFS image.
.TP
\f[B]build\-modules\f[R]
Build additional SquashFS modules.
.TP
\f[B]build\-boot\f[R]
Generate boot files, initrd, and boot\-loader configuration.
.TP
\f[B]build\-config\f[R]
Generate live\-system configuration data.
.TP
\f[B]build\-iso\f[R]
Create the final ISO from prepared build data.
.TP
\f[B]remove\-sources\f[R]
If \f[B]REMOVE_SOURCES=true\f[R], delete and recreate the complete
selected work directory.
Otherwise this stage does nothing.
.SH RANGE SELECTION
No arguments, \f[B]\-h\f[R], or \f[B]\-\-help\f[R] display help.
.PP
A single command runs only that stage.
\f[B]start\-command \- end\-command\f[R] runs an inclusive range.
\f[B]\- end\-command\f[R] starts at the first stage.
\f[B]start\-command \-\f[R] continues through the final stage.
A lone \f[B]\-\f[R] runs every stage.
.SH EXAMPLES
Run the complete build:
.IP
.EX
sudo minios\-live \-
.EE
.PP
Run from the first stage through chroot installation:
.IP
.EX
sudo minios\-live \- build\-chroot
.EE
.PP
Rebuild boot and configuration data:
.IP
.EX
sudo minios\-live build\-boot \- build\-config
.EE
.PP
Create an ISO from prepared data:
.IP
.EX
sudo minios\-live build\-iso
.EE
.SH CONFIGURATION
A source checkout reads \f[B]linux\-live/build.conf\f[R] by default and
uses \f[B]build/\f[R] below the checkout.
An installed copy reads \f[B]/etc/minios\-live/build.conf\f[R] and uses
\f[B]build/\f[R] below the current directory.
Set \f[B]BUILD_CONF\f[R] and \f[B]BUILD_DIR\f[R] to override those
defaults.
.PP
Configuration files are sourced as Bash and must be trusted.
.PP
Additional software is selected in module \f[B]packages.list\f[R] files.
Modules are linked into the selected environment under
\f[B]linux\-live/environments/\f[R].
.PP
\f[B]build\-modules\f[R] skips modules whose SquashFS artifacts already
exist.
After changing a module, remove its artifact from the selected work
directory\[cq]s \f[B]image/\f[R] tree before rebuilding.
The builder then invalidates the following module chain; kernel module
rebuilding is handled separately.
.SH FILES
.TP
\f[B]linux\-live/build.conf\f[R]
Default configuration in a source checkout.
.TP
\f[B]/etc/minios\-live/build.conf\f[R]
Default configuration for an installed copy.
.TP
\f[B]linux\-live/prerequisites.list\f[R]
Host packages required for a source\-tree build.
